  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional and Systems Strengthening (ISS) Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Uganda):  The Feed the Future Institutional and Systems Strengthening Activity will build the capacity and systems of key national-level inistries, departments and agencies (MDAs) and industry apex organizations (IAOs) that are vital to driving agricultural sector growth, including improving the safety of food supply across agriculture value chains. The Activity will support these entities to improve their internal processes, enabling them to better fulfill their mandates. The Activity will focus on key entry points within the MDAs&apos; and IAOs&apos; structures and systems to optimize functionality, inclusiveness, and adoption of innovative approaches to spur agriculture sector development, including increased production, quality, and safety of food important for nutrition.With FY 2022 funds, activities will include public-private sector dialogue to bring about desired reforms and encourage participation in policy implementation. These activities will promote behavioral change in selected MDAs and IAOs through: 1) ongoing institutional self-assessments and implementation of improvement action plans, 2) platforms for collaboration among market actors, 3) capacity building for strategic communication, 4) human resource capacity development, and 5) uptake of digital solutions for efficient service delivery. The Activity will also deploy grants as a tool to incentivize adoption of innovative business models and approaches to service delivery among the IAOs and MDAs.The activity will contribute to the Gender Equity and Equality Action (GEEA) Fund Priority 5: Dismantling systemic barriers through building the capacity of ministries, departments, agencies, and industry apex organizations to carry out gender responsive planning, programming, and budgeting. It will support the development, review, and implementation of gender strategies at the National Meteorological Authority; Ministry of Trade, Industry and Cooperatives; and the Equal Opportunities Commission...</narrative>
  </description>
